WEBVTT

00:00:03.279 --> 00:00:06.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me all right?</v>

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, bit tinny, but that might be this headset.</v>

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.640
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sounds normal to me.</v>

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.089
<v Jamie Brennan>Ah. Just my bargain headset, then.</v>

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we've got everyone. Marcus, you look like you've only just sat down.</v>

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:31.699
<v Marcus Hale>I have. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. Spent longer looking at the same van than I did driving.</v>

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:34.159
<v Callum Reid>Coming past the retail park?</v>

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:39.579
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah. Absolutely solid, then nothing. No obvious reason for it.</v>

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:41.990
<v Fiona Doyle>Standard Tuesday, that.</v>

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:46.659
<v Tomasz Nowak>At least you had a nice view of a van.</v>

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Callum, do you want to start us off?</v>

00:00:52.590 --> 00:01:01.340
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, the run to Tollgate for the replacement parts for the line one HPU — all done. Picked them up and they're back here.</v>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Callum.</v>

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:11.170
<v Callum Reid>And just an observation from nights: noticed the main conveyor was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.489
<v Aisha Begum>Warm towards the start of the shift, you mean?</v>

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:21.069
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, earlier on. Nothing sustained. It was back to normal afterwards.</v>

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.689
<v Tomasz Nowak>Mm, okay. Nights can feel warm in there even when it's freezing outside.</v>

00:01:28.319 --> 00:01:29.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, understood. Jamie?</v>

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:37.200
<v Jamie Brennan>Only that we tested the line 1 TCU yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished.</v>

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. Nice to hear 'fine' for a change.</v>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.569
<v Jamie Brennan>I know. Nearly didn't recognise the word myself.</v>

00:01:46.879 --> 00:01:48.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, over to you.</v>

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:57.609
<v Fiona Doyle>My investigation into the pressure drop on the BFP isn't happening now. The other shift already sorted it, so that's cancelled.</v>

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough, thanks.</v>

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, where are you with yours?</v>

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:12.289
<v Marcus Hale>The purchase order chase — I've had a first look, nothing major so far. Still working through it, though.</v>

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.599
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, understood.</v>

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.800
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, Jamie, thought you were coming in with something.</v>

00:02:22.389 --> 00:02:24.490
<v Jamie Brennan>No, just agreeing. Rare, I know.</v>

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:33.469
<v Sarah Okafor>And Marcus asked me to pass on that the contractor booking is moving from him to me. I'll take that on.</v>

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.240
<v Marcus Hale>Thanks, boss. Appreciate that.</v>

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:40.759
<v Aisha Begum>Jamie agreeing and the boss taking the phone calls. Unusual morning.</v>

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't get used to it. Right, two new bits.</v>

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.610
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll send the shift handover report round by Wednesday. Normal priority on that.</v>

00:02:52.259 --> 00:02:53.659
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, Sarah, that works.</v>

00:02:55.349 --> 00:03:01.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, can you sort the training records for the new starters, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:07.520
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters when I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. No rush on those.</v>

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:14.569
<v Aisha Begum>I'm still putting faces to names with the new starters.</v>

00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:18.409
<v Callum Reid>Helmets on, specs on, everybody looks vaguely like somebody else.</v>

00:03:19.569 --> 00:03:24.469
<v Tomasz Nowak>Then you see them in the car park and don't recognise them at all.</v>

00:03:25.759 --> 00:03:29.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I've had people walk straight past me without the hi-vis.</v>

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.229
<v Jamie Brennan>You sure that's why?</v>

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:35.539
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Cheers, Jamie. Very supportive.</v>

00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:40.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes personal — anything else new we need in here?</v>

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.800
<v Aisha Begum>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:03:45.949 --> 00:03:47.349
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, I'm all right.</v>

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.460
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nothing to add here either.</v>

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.900
<v Fiona Doyle>We're good from planning.</v>

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, we'll leave it there. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.349
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.090
<v Jamie Brennan>See you in a bit.</v>
